# Move the drone's own camera in the body frame.
#
# `pitch` is the one that matters and the one that has cost the most time: at -28.6 deg,
# level flight sits in the top 13.7% of the frame, so a backend that does not know the goal
# ALTITUDE will fly itself into the ground. Changing it invalidates comparisons against
# every episode scored at the old value - it is a measurement surface, not a preference.
float64[3] xyz                  # metres, body FRD, from the vehicle origin
float64 roll                    # RADIANS
float64 pitch                   # RADIANS - this file said "degrees" and it was wrong.
float64 yaw                     # RADIANS
#
# The values go unchanged to `airsim.to_quaternion(pitch, roll, yaw)`
# (sim_bridge/carla_air/camera.py:50), which takes radians. `configs/testbed.yaml` already
# calls its own default `episode_pitch_rad`, and run_episode.py's --camera-pitch is radians.
# Only this comment disagreed, and it is the only documentation a client reading the interface
# ever sees.
#
# Cost of the wrong comment, measured: a client passed -28.6 believing degrees. -28.6 RADIANS
# normalises to -198.6 deg, so the camera turned almost all the way round and stared at the
# aircraft's own airframe from in front, at 0.8 m. Every frame the model saw was rotors and
# fuselage, and three separate conclusions were drawn from that view before anyone opened a
# frame and looked at it.
---
bool success
string message
